\"Healthy but slow selected instance is rendered stale by the 3x-interval freshness window\",\n  \"spec\": \"Problem: pageView uses 3*refreshInterval as expiry, but refreshLoop waits the interval AFTER collection completes. With default selected interval 2s, snapshots expire after 6s while a legitimate collection can run up to refreshTimeout=30s. This is a missed-refresh signal calculated from an incomplete cycle budget.\\n\\nScope: derive the missed-refresh budget from the configured wait interval plus the existing total collection deadline, with a small documented scheduling allowance. Use existing timing constants and one authoritative calculation; add no persisted duration measurement, extra ticker, or per-instance configuration. Preserve immediate stale on explicit collection error and unknown before any successful snapshot. A silent/stuck worker must still expire even without an error; do not suppress staleness merely because an attempt started. Preserve visible observation timestamps.\\n\\nProof: deterministic time-controlled tests through pageView/real templates show a prior-success selected instance stays fresh beyond the old 6s threshold while within its legitimate cycle budget, becomes stale at the new expiry boundary, and is stale immediately on explicit error. No-success remains unknown. Cover selected/fleet interval changes without sleeps. Exercise one slow-success collector scenario and show eventual successful refresh, with no overlapping collection. Run existing checks. This job owns the elapsed-time regression proposed by canopy-tester-freshness-elapsed-decay; do not pin the obsolete 3x-interval formula.\",\n  \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\n  \"lease\": {\n    \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"principal\": \"none\",\n    \"until\": \"2026-09-04T23:45:59.304Z\"\n  },\n  \"ask\": null,\n  \"proof\": null,\n  \"abandoned\": false,\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:56.656Z\",\n      \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n      \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy worktree 1788550542915580458-critic, git c203dc9118ace7575d8aab1162f11edc2e3b601a (running build revision unknown)\\nObserved: view.go:172 passes maxAge = 3*a.refreshInterval(instance.ID) to instanceView, and view.go:155-157 classifies an instance Stale when now \\u003e= LastSuccess+maxAge even with state.Err == nil. For the selected instance, refreshInterval is SelectedIntervalSeconds (default 2s, inventory.go:27), so the staleness window is 6s. A successful Collect (collector.go:131-208) runs 4+N subprocesses (version, config show, declaration list, one declaration show per declaration, status), each individually bounded by a 30s timeout (collector.go:17, app.go:16), so a healthy selected instance — especially over SSH — can routinely take longer than 6s per cycle. Result: templates/instance.html:16 and fleet.html:21 render the \\\"stale\\\" badge/state-dot for an instance whose collection is succeeding with no error, contradicting the README boundary that stale marks failed/missed refreshes, not healthy ones.\\nRequired: freshness must not report stale for an instance whose refreshes are succeeding; the missed-refresh window must exceed the worst-case collection time for that instance.\\nProposed spec direction: derive maxAge from the collection bound (e.g. refreshTimeout plus margin, or observed last cycle duration) instead of 3x the poll interval, or measure and store per-instance refresh cycle duration; pin with a test where a selected instance with a slow but successful collector renders fresh, not stale.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:45:59.304Z\",\n      \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n      \"text\": \"took\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"created_by\": \"none\",\n  \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n  \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:44:02.78Z\",\n  \"promotions\": [\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:44:02.78Z\",\n      \"by\": \"none\",\n      \"spec\": \"Problem: pageView uses 3*refreshInterval as expiry, but refreshLoop waits the interval AFTER collection completes. With default selected interval 2s, snapshots expire after 6s while a legitimate collection can run up to refreshTimeout=30s. This is a missed-refresh signal calculated from an incomplete cycle budget.\\n\\nScope: derive the missed-refresh budget from the configured wait interval plus the existing total collection deadline, with a small documented scheduling allowance. Use existing timing constants and one authoritative calculation; add no persisted duration measurement, extra ticker, or per-instance configuration. Preserve immediate stale on explicit collection error and unknown before any successful snapshot. A silent/stuck worker must still expire even without an error; do not suppress staleness merely because an attempt started. Preserve visible observation timestamps.\\n\\nProof: deterministic time-controlled tests through pageView/real templates show a prior-success selected instance stays fresh beyond the old 6s threshold while within its legitimate cycle budget, becomes stale at the new expiry boundary, and is stale immediately on explicit error. No-success remains unknown. Cover selected/fleet interval changes without sleeps. Exercise one slow-success collector scenario and show eventual successful refresh, with no overlapping collection. Run existing checks. This job owns the elapsed-time regression proposed by canopy-tester-freshness-elapsed-decay; do not pin the obsolete 3x-interval formula.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:32.492Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:45:59.304Z\",\n  \"derived\": {\n    \"terminal\": false,\n    \"waiting\": false,\n    \"open\": true,\n    \"live\": true,\n    \"takeable\": false\n  }\n}\n===\ntotal 168\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 phaedrus phaedrus   532 Sep  4 14:45 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 phaedrus phaedrus   110 Sep  4 14:45 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 phaedrus phaedrus    78 Sep  4 14:45 agents\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus  9302 Sep  4 14:45 app.go\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus  7825 Sep  4 14:45 app_test.go\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus   466 Sep  4 14:45 canopy.example.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus 14988 Sep  4 14:45 collector.go\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus  8074 Sep  4 14:45 collector_test.go\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus  5943 Sep  4 14:45 discovery.go\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus  4932 Sep  4 14:45 discovery_test.go\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus   430 Sep  4 14:45 forest.yaml\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus    96 Sep  4 14:45 .git\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus    35 Sep  4 14:45 .gitignore\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus    25 Sep  4 14:45 go.mod\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus  8767 Sep  4 14:45 inventory.go\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus  2333 Sep  4 14:45 inventory_test.go\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus  2451 Sep  4 14:45 main.go\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus  8705 Sep  4 14:45 model.go\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus  2510 Sep  4 14:45 README.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus  6990 Sep  4 14:45 server.go\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus 16286 Sep  4 14:45 server_test.go\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 phaedrus phaedrus    42 Sep  4 14:45 static\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 phaedrus phaedrus    80 Sep  4 14:45 templates\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus  1078 Sep  4 14:45 templates_test.go\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus   678 Sep  4 14:45 THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES\n-rw-r--r-- 1 phaedrus phaedrus 13440 Sep  4 14:45 view.go\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788551163217},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.encrypted\",\"data\":\"Q-PaDgEjlmHZMDgbOfLDvyGDDkdtfsQ1iZKEDIk03dQ9qFRbuz4E51RKNx_dAG0QA0Lt2aaLVYi3uOiDSVpFh1hBFxFXmciDpPfL819POnJQUV4xctEIzE2CcBZk2aqSJEqa0kjnNRBAe3KVDjQZftd7dsGohOqp4qX7xMlbqcpTxdAdtTcuj5UW8fCi6yQhQYg0WBjmu5CFy8J1fMsGgMvjPSKnkmjsn5DW1yvowfSgz0OJvCAFRtZWinZgSmULEByVAKOpJdhfgrwT9P5FkttCuoFYKd8Ef5nK6mAph7SdcHs2F5_CuiHwnZQ8sw54lJrvbgXvdnSN3ITrGUkVnWFQN6XdRUkN